+### Compute pipelines built on the submit thread at their first dispatch
+
+- **Symptom:** frames of 2-4 s on entering a new area, with `[longframe]` naming `new pipelines 14-16` and 2,400-4,300 ms "in all", while the pipeline line counts only 20 render draws that waited, 425 ms in all. On a first start after an install the title holds for minutes. With the Metal shader cache set aside the same route logs `compute pipeline <key>: 1,210 ms on the submit thread at its first dispatch`, and the title movie's network kernels 58-83 s each.
+- **Cause:** a compute shader's pipeline was made with `newComputePipelineStateWithFunction` at its first dispatch, on the submit thread: no stand-in exists for a dispatch, as the hybrid pipelines are for draws, and the pipeline archives held render bases only, so the Metal shader cache was all that stood between the dispatch and a cold compile (20-40 ms warm, 100-1,200 ms cold, the HMMA kernels a minute). Ocarina of Time's effects bring about 20 new compute shaders with each area.
+- **Fix:** `cps_make` in `nvn_mtl.m` takes a compute pipeline from the archives first, the bundled one and this Mac's files (`MTL4Archive newComputePipelineStateWithDescriptor`, about 0.3 ms), else compiles it through the flush period's compiler so the flush writes it into the archive, else the device as before; the prewarm's `C` items and the dispatch go through it. `pso_offline.py` puts every compute shader of the shader map into the bundled archive (`--compute`, the profile's map with `--game`; metal-tt's `compute_pipeline_descriptors`), so a packed app never compiles a compute pipeline at play. The prefetch at program creation (`mtl_prog_prefetch`) builds the compute pipeline too, through the same path, and a dispatch that comes first takes a queued build over instead of waiting behind the hundreds a scene load queues (`DM_NVN_PREFETCH_CPS=0` turns that part off); it helps only when the program is made well before its first dispatch.
+- **Check:** `t_pso_archive`, `t_pso_bundle`, `t_pso_warm`, `test_pso_offline.py`. On the Mac, set the app's Metal cache aside (`$(getconf DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR)/<bundle id>/com.apple.metal`) and run a scripted route with an empty `DM_PSO_USER` list: the `compute pipeline … on the submit thread` lines and the pipeline line's `compute pipelines from the archives N` say where each one came from.
+- **Found on:** [The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time](../../dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md#found-on-this-game): a 25-minute session had four frames of 2.2-4.4 s, all on entering a new area; a cold-cache route to Kokiri Forest spent 195 s of its submit thread in pipelines, 155 s of it in the title's twelve compute kernels.
